description:
**Problem:** cxf_addconstr uses O(nnz) insertion for each coefficient.

**Profile data (ship04l):**
- cxf_addconstr: 10.45% of total runtime (55M instructions)

**Root cause (constr_stub.c:101-116):**
```c
/* For each coefficient insertion: */
/* Shift ALL subsequent entries right by 1 */
for (int64_t k = matrix->nnz; k > col_end; k--) {
    matrix->row_idx[k] = matrix->row_idx[k - 1];
    matrix->values[k] = matrix->values[k - 1];
}
/* Update ALL column pointers after this one */
for (int j = col + 1; j <= matrix->num_cols; j++) {
    matrix->col_ptr[j]++;
}
```

For 6,332 coefficients, total is O(nnz^2).

**Solution:** Buffer (row, col, val) triplets, sort by column, build CSC in one pass.

**Expected savings:** ~8% total runtime reduction.
